/-!
# Stacks 0DXW: a principal ideal generated by a nonzerodivisor

Fix an algebraization situation (Stacks 0EHC): a Noetherian ring `A` with ideals `I ⊆ 𝔞`, the
affine scheme `X = Spec(A)`, the closed subscheme `Y = V(I)` and the open complement
`U = X ∖ V(𝔞)`. Let `(F_n)` be an object of `Coh(U, I𝒪_U)`, a coherent `I`-adic system on `U`.
Stacks 0DXW assumes

1. `I = (f)` is the principal ideal generated by a nonzerodivisor `f ∈ 𝔞`,
2. `F_n` is a finite locally free `𝒪_U/f^n𝒪_U`-module,
3. `H¹_𝔞(A/fA)` and `H²_𝔞(A/fA)` are finite `A`-modules,

and concludes that `(F_n)` extends canonically to `X`, and that if `A` is `I`-adically complete
then `(F_n)` is the completion of a coherent `𝒪_U`-module.

Both conclusions are proved here, from those three conditions and nothing else.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Algebraization.exists_pow_smul_factor_firstTerm` — the factorization condition of
  Local Cohomology 0BPY over the base module `A/fA`, for the module algebraizing `F_1`: for
  every `g ∈ 𝔞` some power of `g` on that module factors through a finite free `A/fA`-module.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.finite_complementCohomologyBase_firstTerm` — the finiteness of
  `H^p(U, F_1)` for `p < s`, in the local-cohomology spelling, from the finiteness of
  `H^i_𝔞(A/fA)` for `1 ≤ i ≤ s`; condition (3) is the case `s = 2`.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.canonicallyExtends_and_isCompletion_of_principal_nonzerodivisor` —
  **Stacks 0DXW**, both clauses.

## Implementation notes

The two global steps of the source's proof are already in the library: the short exact sequences
`0 → F_n → F_{n+1} → F_1 → 0` are
`Stacks.Algebraization.hasPrincipalShortExactSequences_of_locallyFree`, and from them together
with the finiteness of `H⁰(U, F_1)` and `H¹(U, F_1)` the two conclusions are
`Stacks.Algebraization.canonicallyExtends_of_principal_shortExactSequences` — the Mittag-Leffler
criterion Stacks 0EHH — and
`Stacks.Algebraization.isCompletionNearClosed_of_principal_shortExactSequences`. What this file
adds is the derivation of that finiteness from condition (3), which the source gets from Local
Cohomology 0BK0 and 0BLT, by a route that avoids 0BLT:

* `F_1` is `M^~|_U` for a finite `A`-module `M` annihilated by `f`
  (`Stacks.Algebraization.exists_finiteModule_smul_eq_zero_tilde_restrict_iso`), so `M` is a
  finite module over `B = A/fA`;
* conditions (1) and (2) make `M` locally free over `B`
  (`Stacks.Algebraization.free_localizedModule_baseQuotient`), so for every `g ∈ 𝔞` a power of
  `g` on `M` factors through a finite free `B`-module
  (`Stacks.BaseQuotientFactorization.exists_pow_smul_factor_through_baseQuotient'`);
* that factorization transports the finiteness of the local cohomology of `A/fA` given by
  condition (3) to the local cohomology of `M`, which is Local Cohomology 0BPY over the base
  module `A/fA` (`Stacks.LocalCohomology.localCohomologyWithSupportIn_finite_of_base`);
* and 0BK0 reads that back as the finiteness of `H⁰(U, F_1)` and `H¹(U, F_1)`.

Condition (2) is `Stacks.Algebraization.IsFiniteLocallyFreeAdic` applied to
`Stacks.Algebraization.idealOnOpen`, and condition (3) is the finiteness of
`Stacks.Algebraization.localCohomologyBaseQuotient` in degrees `1` and `2`; both readings are
discussed in the sibling module `PrincipalNonzerodivisorHypotheses` of
`StacksDraft.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.CompletionCriteria`.

The second clause is stated as membership in the essential image of the completion functor of
Stacks 0EKZ, which is what "is the completion of a coherent `𝒪_U`-module" means for a system on
`U`; the equivalence with the near-closed formulation is
`Stacks.Algebraization.isCompletion_iff_nearClosed`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DXW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DXW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EHH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EHH)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EHC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EHC)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BK0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BK0)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BPY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BPY)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0H39](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0H39)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite
open Stacks.ModuleSkyscraper
open scoped AlgebraicGeometry

universe u

namespace Stacks.Algebraization

variable (S : AlgebraizationSituation.{u})
  (F : Stacks.Coherent.CoherentAdicSystems (idealOnOpen S))

/-! ### The factorization condition of Stacks 0BPY over the base module `A/fA` -/

/-- **The factorization condition of Local Cohomology 0BPY over the base module `A/fA`.** Let
`(F_n)` be a coherent `I`-adic system on `U` whose terms are finite locally free over the
infinitesimal neighbourhoods, with `I = (f)`, and let `M` be a finite `A`-module annihilated by
`f` whose associated sheaf restricts on `U` to the first term `F_1`. Then for every `g ∈ 𝔞` some
power of `g` on `M` factors through a finite free `A/fA`-module.

Multiplication by `g` on `M` is a unit after localizing at any prime `𝔭` of `A` which avoids `g`;
such a prime does not contain `𝔞`, so it is the prime under a point of `U`, and conditions (1)
and (2) make `M` free over `A/fA` localized there
(`Stacks.Algebraization.free_localizedModule_baseQuotient`). Local freeness over the basic open
of `g` is exactly what
`Stacks.BaseQuotientFactorization.exists_pow_smul_factor_through_baseQuotient'` turns into the
factorization. -/
theorem exists_pow_smul_factor_firstTerm (f : S.A) (hI : S.I = Ideal.span {f})
    (hfreeAdic : IsFiniteLocallyFreeAdic (idealOnOpen S) F)
    (M : ModuleCat.{u} (CommRingCat.of S.A)) [Module.Finite S.A (M : Type u)]
    (hfM : ∀ x : (M : Type u), f • x = 0)
    (e : (AlgebraicGeometry.tilde M).restrict S.U.ι ≅ systemObj S F 0) :
    ∀ g ∈ S.a, ∃ (k d : ℕ)
        (a : (Fin d → ((baseQuotient S f : ModuleCat.{u} S.A) : Type u)) →ₗ[S.A] (M : Type u))
        (b : (M : Type u) →ₗ[S.A] (Fin d → ((baseQuotient S f : ModuleCat.{u} S.A) : Type u))),
      a ∘ₗ b = g ^ k • LinearMap.id := by
  intro g hg
  refine Stacks.BaseQuotientFactorization.exists_pow_smul_factor_through_baseQuotient'
    f g (M : Type u) hfM fun p _ q _ hq hgp hfp => ?_
  let : Module (S.A ⧸ Ideal.span {f}) (M : Type u) :=
    Module.IsTorsionBy.module (R := S.A) (M := (M : Type u)) (r := f) (fun ⦃x⦄ => hfM x)
  have : IsScalarTower S.A (S.A ⧸ Ideal.span {f}) (M : Type u) := isScalarTower_isTorsionBy hfM
  exact free_localizedModule_baseQuotient S F f hI hfreeAdic M hfM e p q hq
    (fun h => hgp (h hg)) hfp

/-! ### The finiteness of the cohomology of the first term -/

/-- **The finiteness of `H^p(U, F_1)` for `p < s`, in the local-cohomology spelling.** If
`H^i_𝔞(A/fA)` is a finite `A`-module for `1 ≤ i ≤ s`, and if some power of every `g ∈ 𝔞` on the
finite `A`-module `M` factors through a finite free `A/fA`-module, then `H^p(U, M^~)` is a finite
`A`-module for every `p < s`.

At `s = 2` the finiteness hypothesis is condition (3) of Stacks 0DXW and the conclusion covers
`H^0(U, F_1)` and `H^1(U, F_1)`, which is what that tag's proof needs. At `s = 1` it is the
degree-`≤ 1` finiteness that hypothesis (5) of [Stacks, Tag 0DXU] supplies through
[Stacks, Tag 0EFD], and the conclusion covers `H^0(U, F_1)` alone — which is condition (c) of
[Stacks, Tag 0EHH], all that the proof of that tag asks of its hypothesis (5).

In degree `0` the finiteness of the local cohomology is automatic
(`Stacks.LocalCohomology.finite_localCohomologyWithSupportIn_of_nonpos`). The factorization of
`Stacks.Algebraization.exists_pow_smul_factor_firstTerm` carries the finiteness from the base
module `A/fA` to `M` by Local Cohomology 0BPY over a base module, and Local Cohomology 0BK0 (3)
reads the result back as finiteness of the cohomology on `U`. -/
theorem finite_complementCohomologyBase_firstTerm (f : S.A)
    (M : ModuleCat.{u} (CommRingCat.of S.A)) [Module.Finite S.A (M : Type u)] (s : ℕ)
    (hfin : ∀ i : ℕ, 1 ≤ i → i ≤ s → Module.Finite S.A (localCohomologyBaseQuotient S f i))
    (hM : ∀ g ∈ S.a, ∃ (k d : ℕ)
        (a : (Fin d → ((baseQuotient S f : ModuleCat.{u} S.A) : Type u)) →ₗ[S.A] (M : Type u))
        (b : (M : Type u) →ₗ[S.A] (Fin d → ((baseQuotient S f : ModuleCat.{u} S.A) : Type u))),
      a ∘ₗ b = g ^ k • LinearMap.id) (p : ℕ) (hp : p < s) :
    Module.Finite S.A
      (Stacks.LocalCohomologySequence.complementCohomologyBase (A := CommRingCat.of S.A)
        S.a M p) := by
  have := finite_baseQuotient S f
  have hN : ∀ i : ℕ, i ≤ s → Module.Finite S.A
      (Stacks.LocalCohomology.localCohomologyWithSupportIn.{u, 0} S.A
        (PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (S.a : Set S.A))
        ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} S.A) 0).obj (baseQuotient S f))
        (i : ℤ)) := by
    intro i hi
    rcases Nat.eq_zero_or_pos i with rfl | hi1
    · exact Stacks.LocalCohomology.finite_localCohomologyWithSupportIn_of_nonpos.{u, 0} S.A _
        (baseQuotient S f) 0 le_rfl
    · exact hfin i hi1 hi
  have hbase := Stacks.LocalCohomology.localCohomologyWithSupportIn_finite_of_base
    S.A S.a s (baseQuotient S f) hN (ModuleCat.of S.A (M : Type u)) hM
  rw [Stacks.LocalCohomologySequence.finite_complementCohomologyBase_iff_finite_localCohomology
    (A := CommRingCat.of S.A) S.a M p]
  exact hbase (p + 1) (by omega)

/-! ### Stacks 0DXW -/

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0DXW.** Let `S` be an algebraization situation and let `(F_n)` be a
coherent `I`-adic system on the open complement `U`. Assume

1. `I = (f)` is generated by a nonzerodivisor `f ∈ 𝔞`,
2. every term of the system is finite locally free over the infinitesimal neighbourhood it is
   annihilated by,
3. `H¹_𝔞(A/fA)` and `H²_𝔞(A/fA)` are finite `A`-modules.

Then `(F_n)` extends canonically to `X = Spec(A)`, and if `A` is `I`-adically complete then
`(F_n)` is the completion of a coherent `𝒪_U`-module.

Conditions (1) and (2) give the short exact sequences `0 → F_n → F_{n+1} → F_1 → 0` of the
source's proof (`Stacks.Algebraization.hasPrincipalShortExactSequences_of_locallyFree`), and
all three give the finiteness of `H⁰(U, F_1)` and `H¹(U, F_1)`
(`Stacks.Algebraization.finite_complementCohomologyBase_firstTerm`). The Mittag-Leffler criterion
Stacks 0EHH turns those into the first clause
(`Stacks.Algebraization.canonicallyExtends_of_principal_shortExactSequences`) and the chain of
Stacks 0EIL into the second
(`Stacks.Algebraization.isCompletionNearClosed_of_principal_shortExactSequences`). -/
@[stacks 0DXW "both clauses under the source's own conditions (1), (2) and (3): for I = (f) \
generated by a nonzerodivisor, with every term finite locally free over the infinitesimal \
neighbourhood it is annihilated by, and with H¹_𝔞(A/fA) and H²_𝔞(A/fA) finite, the system \
extends canonically to X, and over an I-adically complete A it is the completion of a coherent \
O_U-module"]
theorem canonicallyExtends_and_isCompletion_of_principal_nonzerodivisor
    (S : AlgebraizationSituation.{u})
    (F : Stacks.Coherent.CoherentAdicSystems (idealOnOpen S)) (f : S.A)
    (hI : S.I = Ideal.span {f}) (hf : f ∈ nonZeroDivisors S.A)
    (hfree : IsFiniteLocallyFreeAdic (idealOnOpen S) F)
    (h₁ : Module.Finite S.A (localCohomologyBaseQuotient S f 1))
    (h₂ : Module.Finite S.A (localCohomologyBaseQuotient S f 2)) :
    CanonicallyExtends S F ∧
      (IsAdicComplete (Ideal.span {f}) S.A →
        (completionFunctor S.U.toScheme (S.Yι.ker.comap S.U.ι)).essImage (kerComapSystem S F)) := by
  obtain ⟨M, hMfin, hfM, ⟨eM⟩⟩ :=
    exists_finiteModule_smul_eq_zero_tilde_restrict_iso S F f hI
  have := hMfin
  have hcomp := finite_complementCohomologyBase_firstTerm S f M 2
    (fun i hi1 hi2 => by interval_cases i; exacts [h₁, h₂])
    (exists_pow_smul_factor_firstTerm S F f hI hfree M hfM eM)
  have hqc : (systemObj S F 0).IsQuasicoherent := F.property.isQuasicoherent 0
  have hopen : ∀ p : ℕ, p < 2 →
      Module.Finite S.A ((openCohomologyFunctor S p).obj (systemObj S F 0)) := fun p hp =>
    finite_openCohomology_of_finite_complementCohomologyBase S (systemObj S F 0) M eM p
      (hcomp p hp)
  have h0 : Module.Finite S.A ((globalSectionsSystem S F).obj (op 0)) :=
    finite_globalSectionsSystem_zero_of_finite_openCohomology S F (hopen 0 (by omega))
  have h1 : Module.Finite S.A ((openCohomologyFunctor S 1).obj (systemObj S F 0)) :=
    hopen 1 (by omega)
  have h : HasPrincipalShortExactSequences S F f :=
    hasPrincipalShortExactSequences_of_locallyFree S F f hI hf hfree
  refine ⟨canonicallyExtends_of_principal_shortExactSequences S F f hI h h0 h1,
    fun hcomplete => (isCompletion_iff_nearClosed S (kerComapSystem S F)).mpr
      (isCompletionNearClosed_of_principal_shortExactSequences S F f hI hcomplete h h0 h1)⟩

end Stacks.Algebraization

end
